{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898224-what-does-it-mean-to-be-redeemed-as-an-abyssal","id":898224,"title":"What does it mean to be Redeemed as an Abyssal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-24T14:34:19-07:00","id":898224,"title":"What does it mean to be Redeemed as an Abyssal?","content":"What happens when an Abyssal becomes a Solar? Does it mean some sort of Karmic debt has been paid? Have sufficient positive Resonance over come the negative? Has the Abyssal attained some sort of enlightenment? Though if I ever play the Abyssal Redemption story it will likely involve the enlightenment that comes from mastering MAs, such as Wood Dragon Style, Solar Hero Style, and Argument of Compassion Style, I really want to know WHY the Abyssal becomes a Solar again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:38:16-07:00","id":898230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898224-what-does-it-mean-to-be-redeemed-as-an-abyssal#post898224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when an Abyssal becomes a Solar? Does it mean some sort of Karmic debt has been paid? Have sufficient positive Resonance over come the negative? Has the Abyssal attained some sort of enlightenment? Though if I ever play the Abyssal Redemption story it will likely involve the enlightenment that comes from mastering MAs, such as Wood Dragon Style, Solar Hero Style, and Argument of Compassion Style, I really want to know WHY the Abyssal becomes a Solar again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the past, it meant that the Neverborn's taint from the Solar shard has been cleaned, and so the Abyssal has returned to its &quot;natural&quot; state of being a Solar. If Abyssals and Solars are two sides of the same coin, it simply means the coin has been flipped back to the Solar side. While the specifics of HOW this &quot;redemption&quot; was achieved remained fluid and mutable from table to table, the general assumption was that the Abyssal would almost certainly have to die in order to facilitate the change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:42:16-07:00","id":898239,"title":"","content":"The character has cultivated and demonstrated the will to be a hero who triumphs over death and the ending of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T16:16:32-07:00","id":898334,"title":"","content":"It means they don't own you anymore. The Deathlords, The Neverborn, Oblivion. You have slipped the leash of resonance and reneged your fate as the killer of all there is.<br /> <br /> As to the exact mechanics this process, I haven't the foggiest. It's the rare situation where I agree with the developers &quot;Less is More&quot; approach to Exalted's Cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T17:11:33-07:00","id":898409,"title":"","content":"What it <b>means</b> personally is for individual STs and players to decide. Thematically I think people like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9453_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9453\" data-vbnamecard=\"9453\">Octopoid</a> , and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar331_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"331\" data-vbnamecard=\"331\">The Revenge of TV Head</a> all have the right of it. By getting redeemed, an Abyssal affirms the ultimate power of life over death. Pretty huge slap in the face of entropy, there. <br /> <br /> In my own campaign, Abyssal redemption, or &quot;Taking Wing&quot; takes two forms: Goldwings and Bonewings. <br /> <br /> Goldwings are those Abyssals who forsake the Black Exaltation entirely and become Solar Exalted again. <br /> <br /> Bonewings cleanse their Exaltations of the Void and become the Exalted of Death. Stewards of the underworld, protectors of the dead, bringers of relief from suffering. Nominally neutral, the Sepulchral Exalted are essentially dark heroes who defend the necessity of death and decay as a source of mercy, memory, and renewal. <br /> <br /> Just under one third of all Abyssal Exalted will become Sepulchral Exalted, which is easier to do than becoming a Goldwing, of which there will be maybe 10. The remaining Loyalist Abyssal Exalted, perfectly happy to be life-negating shits, will go to war with the Bonewings to reclaim their Exaltations for the Void. The Bonewings will want to do the same to the Loyalists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T17:25:27-07:00","id":898425,"title":"","content":"I recall a sidebar in one of the Abyssal books (I will try and find it). The mechanics of how the redemption occurred was up to the ST. However upon being redeemed, if I recall correctly, the abyssal converts 1/2 their charms to Solar charms. They lose 1 point of essence as part of the transformation, but they got to keep the charms with their previous level of essence as a prereq. Also, since this soul was Abyssal and was redeemed, they no longer have the Great Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11769-sabreashe","name":"SabreAshe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T22:28:49-07:00","id":898645,"title":"","content":"I believe the sidebar appeared in a book that added even more solars and abyssals charms maybe one of the books that is focused on the Unconquered Sun...high essence ones from what I recall. But well, one thing to keep in mind, this definition doesn't apply to 3e tho...of course they could change their minds but one thing, they kept talking about since the beginning for the Abyssals of 3e, they won't have mirror charms anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T00:27:07-07:00","id":898729,"title":"","content":"What it means, is the abyssal has become powerful enough to shrug off the chains binding it, and has chosen to 'repent' for themselves, going on this mystic quest as if their very nature was in the wrong, and succeeding.<br /> <br /> It means you're now more solar than solar, free of the curse, and with bookoo bragging rights that you ascended back to glory from the lowest depths.<br /> <br /> Personally, I feel abyssal redemption should be about achieving a singular power and freedom, as an abyssal, but obviously, different tables, different rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11609,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11609-shiney103","user":"Shiney103","date":". 05-25-2016, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11609-shiney103","name":"Shiney103","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T06:53:36-07:00","id":898880,"title":"","content":"I don't think becoming a Solar should require being powerful. It should be... however the ST and player define it, but I see it as a moral or spiritual quest of life triumphing over death and Dark Fate, of learning what it means and meant to be a Solar and trying to live as if you already are one, and rejecting the Underworld for Creation.<br /> <br /> I do agree with what others have said that Abyssals should also have options to be heroic and awesome speakers or champions for the ghosts while still being Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T07:13:47-07:00","id":898888,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure we need the narrative of redemption for Abyssals anymore, tbh.<br /> <br /> Abyssal redemption existed in a world where Abyssals were sharply limited by Resonance and Monstrances, and where the purpose of Abyssal was straight forward (murder the universe). 3rd Edition Abyssals, who serve more complex Deathlords and follow the chivalry of death, are less narratively constrained. They likely don't have Monstrances or something similar to chain them in servitude. If an Abyssal can fundamentally do what they want without getting hit on the nose with a newspaper (or getting slapped with no-save auto-death), there is less need for giving them an &quot;out.&quot;<br /> <br /> To put it another way, a Solar can do what they want with their power, good guy, bad girl, capitalist, whatever. The same is true for Lunars and Dragon-Blooded. If Abyssals too are that &quot;free&quot; then really we just gained another generally playable Exalt type, and why ruin that with the judgmental notion of &quot;redemption?&quot; Redemption says there is something wrong about Abyssals that needs to be changed, and implies a degree of failure if they choose to eschew that path.<br /> <br /> Redemption is an interesting narrative, of course, but it can be stifling for PC Abyssals. In this case, Abyssals narratives might become larger by actually removing the choice itself. If an Abyssal doesn't have the compulsion or the option of becoming something else, maybe they can focus on doing what they want with the power they do have.<br /> <br /> 2nd Edition Abyssals was a choice between being Oblivion's bitch or slipping the leash by becoming Solar.<br /> 3rd Edition Abyssals can be an infinitude of choices by simply leaving a Deathknight to their own conscience and ambition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T07:18:34-07:00","id":898892,"title":"","content":"I prefer the option being there as a possibility, to allow the idea that the Abyssal exaltations can be returned to their original form if somebody wants to badly enough.<br /> <br /> I think Abyssals shouldn't be <i><b>as</b></i> narratively restricted as in 2E, but they should still have restrictions: to be deathly Exalted that are linked to the Void and don't entirely belong in Creation. Their exaltations should still be former Solar essences that were warped from their original form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T08:20:50-07:00","id":898941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898224-what-does-it-mean-to-be-redeemed-as-an-abyssal?p=898888#post898888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put it another way, a Solar can do what they want with their power, good guy, bad girl, capitalist, whatever. The same is true for Lunars and Dragon-Blooded. If Abyssals too are that &quot;free&quot; then really we just gained another generally playable Exalt type, and why ruin that with the judgmental notion of &quot;redemption?&quot; Redemption says there is something wrong about Abyssals that needs to be changed, and implies a degree of failure if they choose to eschew that path.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a moral context, I agree with you. I'd rather have Abyssals playable as themselves than have there be a &quot;right&quot; path and a &quot;wrong&quot; path for them to take. Narratively, however, I believe the possibility of returning to a Solar shard should exist, since that's how they were made (I feel the same way about Infernals, though I would never play an Infernal seeking &quot;redemption,&quot; for values of that word). I think, in 3E, &quot;redemption&quot; might be the wrong word, as it comes with all sorts of ethical baggage. Let's instead call it &quot;default reset&quot;. Some people want their settings customized, some want them restored to factory defaults. Neither choice is right or wrong, and both should be equally supported by the game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T10:22:29-07:00","id":899081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898224-what-does-it-mean-to-be-redeemed-as-an-abyssal?p=898941#post898941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a moral context, I agree with you. I'd rather have Abyssals playable as themselves than have there be a &quot;right&quot; path and a &quot;wrong&quot; path for them to take. Narratively, however, I believe the possibility of returning to a Solar shard should exist, since that's how they were made (I feel the same way about Infernals, though I would never play an Infernal seeking &quot;redemption,&quot; for values of that word). I think, in 3E, &quot;redemption&quot; might be the wrong word, as it comes with all sorts of ethical baggage. Let's instead call it &quot;default reset&quot;. Some people want their settings customized, some want them restored to factory defaults. Neither choice is right or wrong, and both should be equally supported by the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question, then, is how to make it a narrative option without framing it as a good/bad dynamic? The word &quot;redemption&quot; should probably be thrown out the window, in that case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T10:53:41-07:00","id":899138,"title":"","content":"Well, clearly it means the Neverborn have withdrawn their favor in disgust from the pusillanimous and wavering soul of one of their Abyssal chosen. The champion is simply unworthy of their power :loyalist:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:39:59-07:00","id":899203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898224-what-does-it-mean-to-be-redeemed-as-an-abyssal?p=899081#post899081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question, then, is how to make it a narrative option without framing it as a good/bad dynamic? The word &quot;redemption&quot; should probably be thrown out the window, in that case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well first, there's still quite a bit of &quot;bad&quot; as an abyssal. Sure you're not a slave who's bound by Resonance and a monstrance, and the Deathlords are not one dimensional super-bosses anymore. That doesn't change the fact that you're serving the Underworld, which itself is &quot;wrong&quot; and shouldn't exist. You're also running around binding ghosts, peoples souls, to absolute servitude (slavery essentially). Don't even get me started on soulsteel, pounding someone's ghost into a metal where they suffer eternally is NOT morally right, it's not even gray. Lastly, the Underworld is a creepy freaking place. I can foresee several abyssal getting wierded out down there.<br /> <br /> Now, I personally have always loved Abyssals (my favorite Exalt actually). The narrative freedom they're being giving this time around is just going to make them that much cooler. However, I don't believe keeping the ambiguous potential for &quot;redemption&quot; hurts them at all. Most of us will embrace being an abyssal. But it doesn't hurt the narrative for a few to say &quot;this is some freaky shit, and I don't think I can deal with all this... there's gotta be a way out!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 05-25-2016, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:10:04-07:00","id":899239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898224-what-does-it-mean-to-be-redeemed-as-an-abyssal?p=899203#post899203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well first, there's still quite a bit of &quot;bad&quot; as an abyssal. Sure you're not a slave who's bound by Resonance and a monstrance, and the Deathlords are not one dimensional super-bosses anymore. That doesn't change the fact that you're serving the Underworld, which itself is &quot;wrong&quot; and shouldn't exist. You're also running around binding ghosts, peoples souls, to absolute servitude (slavery essentially). Don't even get me started on soulsteel, pounding someone's ghost into a metal where they suffer eternally is NOT morally right, it's not even gray. Lastly, the Underworld is a creepy freaking place. I can foresee several abyssal getting wierded out down there.<br /> <br /> Now, I personally have always loved Abyssals (my favorite Exalt actually). The narrative freedom they're being giving this time around is just going to make them that much cooler. However, I don't believe keeping the ambiguous potential for &quot;redemption&quot; hurts them at all. Most of us will embrace being an abyssal. But it doesn't hurt the narrative for a few to say &quot;this is some freaky shit, and I don't think I can deal with all this... there's gotta be a way out!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if they aren't being called explicitly to murder all Creation, I'm not sure I can view them as inherently more evil than Dynasts who squeeze the wealth and prosperity out of half the world to feed their own lifestyle, including mass enslavement.<br /> <br /> I think even your post is indicative of the larger problem. You see Abyssals as being inherently tied to some really immoral things, and therefore the redemption angle is worthwhile. As I mention above, Dynastic Dragon-blooded are also culpable of some pretty gnarly shit, but we don't expect them to have a redemption angle. Why? Well, first, because this is Exalted, and we somewhat expect bad shit to happen. But, more importantly, because we know Dragon-Bloods get to choose to do whatever the hell they want. They are narratively free to be whatever their players want/need them to be.<br /> <br /> If Abyssals get that level of narrative freedom, I'm not sure they need a redemption story. The existence of Ma Ha Suchi doesn't necessitate Lunar redemption. The Maiden of the Mirthless Smile doesn't necessarily require Abyssal redemption.<br /> <br /> They are the Exalted of the Underworld. Those themes are dark, maybe even horrific. I'm not sure they need to be evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T00:36:40-07:00","id":899823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898224-what-does-it-mean-to-be-redeemed-as-an-abyssal?p=899239#post899239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if they aren't being called explicitly to murder all Creation, I'm not sure I can view them as inherently more evil than Dynasts who squeeze the wealth and prosperity out of half the world to feed their own lifestyle, including mass enslavement.<br /> <br /> I think even your post is indicative of the larger problem. You see Abyssals as being inherently tied to some really immoral things, and therefore the redemption angle is worthwhile. As I mention above, Dynastic Dragon-blooded are also culpable of some pretty gnarly shit, but we don't expect them to have a redemption angle. Why? Well, first, because this is Exalted, and we somewhat expect bad shit to happen. But, more importantly, because we know Dragon-Bloods get to choose to do whatever the hell they want. They are narratively free to be whatever their players want/need them to be.<br /> <br /> If Abyssals get that level of narrative freedom, I'm not sure they need a redemption story. The existence of Ma Ha Suchi doesn't necessitate Lunar redemption. The Maiden of the Mirthless Smile doesn't necessarily require Abyssal redemption.<br /> <br /> They are the Exalted of the Underworld. Those themes are dark, maybe even horrific. I'm not sure they need to be evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I don't feel Abyssals are evil at all. If they still have free will, they still get to choose what kind of person they're going to be. However, the Underworld itself is not a good place. The Deathlords are likely to fit into a category we would call evil by our sense of morality. I simply don't think the Neverborn or the Deathlords are going to choose Snow White as an Abyssal. They're going to exalt someone who's far more wolf then sheep, pardon the metaphor.<br /> <br /> I don't see a reason for redemption not to exist. Regardless most of us Abyssal players don't care. We don't play Abyssals because we eventually want to be Solars. We play Abyssals because we enjoy playing as Abyssals!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T02:07:24-07:00","id":899872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/898224-what-does-it-mean-to-be-redeemed-as-an-abyssal?p=899239#post899239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The existence of Ma Ha Suchi doesn't necessitate Lunar redemption.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bEspecially not now that he mostly just keeps to himself.<br /> <br /> I don't think Abyssals would be essentially evil, or for those who personally are that they would necessarily be worse than imperialist Dragon Blooded, but I think there should be something to them running on death and curses that makes those things more than just amoral tools. I think Abyssals should have a quality of being... taboo, untouchable. Grim.<br /> <br /> Not about killing the world (which, really, how did they even do that), but being figures risen from the grave to preside over how it might be ending on its own.<br /> <br /> I think many or most Abyssals buy into that at the start, but some of them might choose something else along the way; they think there's life in the old dog yet, and would like to throw their lot in on that side.<br /> <br /> Heh, all of that gives me an idea of how to alter the Lady of Darkness in Bloodstained Robes, with her previously stated Motivation of destroying those who think themselves righteous; that she thinks it's wrong for heroes like the Solar Exalted to spread false hope in a dying world, and so opposes them and casts them down so that people can embrace the ending, providing solace and succour for those who do. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}